1. Definitions

"The author" is Manuel Mezzanotte.

"The source code" is everything in this repository and in its history,
except the parts listed in section 5.

"The app" is Keel as a program ready to run (Keel.app, and the disk images
and archives that contain it) as published by the author at
https://keel.mezzalab.eu, together with its updates.


2. The source code

You may read the source code, on GitHub or in a copy that GitHub's own
features make, such as a fork, for your own information and study.

Without the author's written permission, you may not, in whole or in part:

  a. copy the source code anywhere outside GitHub;
  b. modify it, translate it, or make works based on it;
  c. build it, run it, or use programs that anyone but the author built
     from it (the app the author publishes is covered by section 3);
  d. publish, distribute, sublicense, rent, lease or sell it;
  e. include it in other software, products or services, free or paid;
  f. use it to train or improve machine learning or AI models.

Forking this repository on GitHub, which GitHub's Terms of Service allow,
gives no rights beyond those in this section.


3. The app

You may download the app from https://keel.mezzalab.eu, install it on any
number of your own computers and use it free of charge, for personal use
and for work, including to write software that you sell. What you make with
Keel is yours.

Without the author's written permission, you may not:

  a. share, publish or distribute the app, or offer it for download
     anywhere else;
  b. sell, rent or lease the app, or charge for it in any way;
  c. modify the app, or reverse engineer, decompile or disassemble it,
     except where the law allows it regardless of this license;
  d. remove or change its notices, this license and the third-party notices
     among them.


